WEBVTT

00:02.890 --> 00:04.400
I'm late!

00:04.400 --> 00:06.370
What's wrong, Otoya?

00:07.730 --> 00:08.630
That was perfect.

00:08.630 --> 00:08.980
Indeed.

00:08.980 --> 00:10.050
Sorry.

00:10.050 --> 00:12.600
Otoya, isn't your meeting today?

00:12.600 --> 00:14.210
That's why I'm in a hurry.

00:14.210 --> 00:15.140
Unbelievable.

00:15.140 --> 00:16.660
Typical Ittoki.

00:16.660 --> 00:18.530
He's full of energy again today.

00:18.530 --> 00:20.430
Ikki, take care.

00:20.430 --> 00:22.090
Go knock it out of the park.

00:22.090 --> 00:23.540
Good luck.

00:25.830 --> 00:29.000
Thanks! I'm off!

02:10.470 --> 02:11.900
Ittoki Otoya.

02:12.300 --> 02:14.150
Do you believe in fate?

02:14.150 --> 02:14.930
Huh?

02:14.930 --> 02:18.030
I'm feeling it right now.

02:18.750 --> 02:20.870
You and I were meant to sing a duet together.

02:22.130 --> 02:23.660
This is fate!

02:24.740 --> 02:26.450
What is he talking about?

02:27.260 --> 02:29.310
Call me Eiichi.

02:29.930 --> 02:31.580
Let's try to be friends.

02:33.430 --> 02:35.000
Right, Otoya?

02:35.000 --> 02:36.380
O-Okay...

02:37.720 --> 02:41.800
By the way, Otoya, what have you
thought of the duet project so far?

02:41.800 --> 02:45.540
M-My thoughts? Everyone's been amazing.

02:45.540 --> 02:47.330
So I'm hoping to do just as well.

02:47.330 --> 02:49.190
"Just as well"? That's all?

02:49.190 --> 02:49.820
Huh?

02:50.620 --> 02:51.980
We'll be seeking to sing

02:53.260 --> 02:57.990
a soul-shaking song that will make even
the hearts of the singers tremble.

02:59.520 --> 03:01.430
Soul-shaking?

03:02.770 --> 03:04.880
So far, the duet project has

03:04.880 --> 03:09.770
changed the members of HEAVENS
and STARISH and helped them grow.

03:10.340 --> 03:13.460
We'll likely grow through
working on the project as well.

03:14.450 --> 03:16.660
But is that enough?

03:17.400 --> 03:19.420
No, of course not.

03:20.550 --> 03:23.260
We'll aim for greater heights than anyone!

03:24.390 --> 03:26.180
Greater heights than anyone?

03:26.180 --> 03:32.280
We'll release our souls sleeping deep
inside our hearts to reach new levels.

03:32.280 --> 03:39.440
Does that mean you'd like to sing
something unlike what you've sung before?

03:39.440 --> 03:40.920
That's exactly right.

03:41.330 --> 03:42.560
Write us something stronger,

03:42.560 --> 03:45.990
deeper, and more intense
than anything you've ever written.

03:46.620 --> 03:48.620
Don't you want the same thing, Otoya?

03:48.620 --> 03:52.100
Yeah. I want to grow as much as the other guys.

03:52.520 --> 03:55.040
I want to try my hand at a soul-shaking song!

03:57.490 --> 03:59.760
I knew we would get along.

04:00.490 --> 04:02.780
I'm starving.

04:02.780 --> 04:04.430
Should we make some curry, then?

04:06.120 --> 04:08.150
HEAVENS is perfect again today.

04:08.150 --> 04:11.970
What? You're creepy
when you're in a good mood.

04:12.930 --> 04:14.140
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

04:14.140 --> 04:16.230
Yeah, I am.

04:18.590 --> 04:19.940
Everything is coming along well.

04:19.940 --> 04:21.550
What's he talking about?

04:21.550 --> 04:23.950
My brother's happy his duet project has started.

04:24.450 --> 04:27.830
I feel intense waves emanating from Eiichi.

04:27.830 --> 04:30.540
Your unusually high level
of excitement is annoying.

04:35.210 --> 04:36.340
Wh-What's going on?

04:36.340 --> 04:37.630
I'm cold.

04:46.750 --> 04:49.440
You must be awfully confident
if you have time for idle talk.

04:51.180 --> 04:59.320
The duet project exists so you can prove
to STARISH that you're better than they are.

05:00.440 --> 05:05.920
HEAVENS is growing towards
heights no one ever imagined.

05:06.740 --> 05:10.990
Growing? That's not what I want!

05:12.010 --> 05:17.250
Move your bodies only
in pursuit of becoming the best.

05:17.250 --> 05:18.630
Breathe only so you can win.

05:18.630 --> 05:21.090
Overwhelm them. Crush them with your dancing.

05:21.090 --> 05:24.050
That is the meaning of your existence!

05:24.050 --> 05:27.630
Results are everything. Show me results.

05:29.600 --> 05:39.400
Riding on this melody we create
together the future becomes today

05:39.400 --> 05:49.110
Like this unchanging phrase
I never want to let you go

05:55.250 --> 05:56.910
This song...

05:57.960 --> 06:04.210
We trip and fall along our way

06:04.710 --> 06:06.920
Tomorrow—

06:06.920 --> 06:08.020
Nanami.

06:08.020 --> 06:11.040
S-Sorry for interrupting you
while you were singing.

06:11.040 --> 06:12.180
Don't worry about it.

06:13.840 --> 06:17.890
That's the first song we wrote together.

06:19.280 --> 06:21.150
I love it.

06:21.150 --> 06:22.570
So do I.

06:23.350 --> 06:25.780
Let's do our best on the duet project, too.

06:26.490 --> 06:28.860
I was surprised by his unexpected request.

06:29.170 --> 06:30.910
But I feel like it's worth doing.

06:32.080 --> 06:33.330
Nanami, you're amazing.

06:33.330 --> 06:34.170
What?

06:34.750 --> 06:37.370
I told Eiichi I wanted to try.

06:38.170 --> 06:40.350
Of course, I wasn't lying.

06:41.180 --> 06:46.620
But I'm actually pretty anxious about
singing a totally new and different song.

06:46.620 --> 06:47.760
Ittoki-kun.

06:49.020 --> 06:52.450
Singing all kinds of songs is fun.

06:53.350 --> 06:56.890
Actually, I guess I was caught
off guard by how intense Eiichi was.

06:56.890 --> 07:00.480
But he really conveyed
how much singing means to him.

07:00.480 --> 07:03.190
Yeah. I can't let him beat me.

07:11.230 --> 07:12.530
What do you think?

07:14.630 --> 07:15.490
Good.

07:15.900 --> 07:18.830
It's exactly what I asked for. No, even better.

07:19.480 --> 07:21.980
It's clearly different
from what we've sung until now.

07:21.980 --> 07:23.250
Thank you.

07:23.650 --> 07:25.210
Otoya, don't you feel the same way?

07:28.710 --> 07:29.970
It's amazing.

07:29.970 --> 07:34.560
Yeah, but we're aiming even higher.

07:34.560 --> 07:35.270
What?

07:35.270 --> 07:38.760
A fantastic song needs a suitable arrangement.

07:39.250 --> 07:43.370
A stronger, more intensely
soul-shaking arrangement.

07:43.370 --> 07:44.310
Okay.

07:44.670 --> 07:47.070
I'm counting on you, Nanami Haruka.

07:48.420 --> 07:50.860
I want to start writing lyrics.

07:52.320 --> 07:56.070
After hearing Nanami's song,
I'm so eager to get started!

07:56.070 --> 07:57.780
Thank you.

07:59.950 --> 08:00.870
Good.

08:01.690 --> 08:03.710
I like that expression, Otoya.

08:03.710 --> 08:08.050
Let's put that excitement
towards writing lyrics.

08:09.130 --> 08:12.170
This will become a soul-shaking song.

08:13.010 --> 08:15.340
I know you and I can do it.

08:15.870 --> 08:16.550
Yeah.

08:20.560 --> 08:23.530
Otoya. Otoya!

08:23.530 --> 08:25.980
Hey, Otoya!

08:29.010 --> 08:30.320
Otoya.

08:30.710 --> 08:31.910
You scared me.

08:31.910 --> 08:33.780
We called you several times.

08:33.780 --> 08:36.200
We're supposed to discuss our next lesson now.

08:36.200 --> 08:40.930
Sorry. I wanted to work on the lyrics
while I waited for you guys to get here.

08:41.590 --> 08:45.710
And the song Nanami wrote
this time gives me goosebumps.

08:45.710 --> 08:47.620
It's amazing.

08:47.620 --> 08:49.750
I need to write lyrics that are just as amazing.

08:49.750 --> 08:53.840
Hold on. Her songs are always the best.

08:53.840 --> 08:58.280
That's right. Haruka's songs are all fantastic.

08:55.690 --> 08:56.720
Okay.

08:58.280 --> 08:59.930
You've got that right.

09:18.960 --> 09:19.870
What are you doing?

09:20.270 --> 09:23.720
Do you really think these lyrics
are good enough for this song?

09:23.720 --> 09:26.330
I poured my heart into those lyrics.

09:26.330 --> 09:29.210
It's not good enough. It's not nearly enough.

09:29.980 --> 09:32.460
These lyrics aren't
a good match for Nanami's song.

09:33.980 --> 09:35.090
But...

09:37.460 --> 09:40.590
This song is a song to shake souls.

09:41.290 --> 09:44.970
It can't be expressed
with surface-level emotions.

09:46.060 --> 09:50.480
Call on the part of yourself
sleeping even deeper inside you.

09:52.820 --> 09:55.260
Deeper inside me?

09:56.530 --> 10:00.700
Abandon your mask of lies
and release your true self.

10:01.920 --> 10:05.540
Otherwise, you won't be able to sing this song.

10:11.400 --> 10:14.840
Look closely at yourself.

10:15.590 --> 10:19.990
Get closer to your true soul.

10:21.620 --> 10:24.430
Will I be able to sing then?

10:25.680 --> 10:31.360
I'm sorry. My head's so full of thoughts
about the song that I was a little hard on you.

10:31.660 --> 10:33.100
No...

10:33.100 --> 10:35.930
But everything is for this song.

10:36.350 --> 10:38.900
It's because I believe in the both of us.

10:39.820 --> 10:40.740
Eiichi.

10:40.740 --> 10:43.740
It's okay. If you're true to yourself,
you can do it.

10:44.820 --> 10:46.950
I'll try again.

10:46.950 --> 10:48.910
Yeah. Let's do our best.

10:54.110 --> 10:56.080
If you're true to yourself, you can do it.

10:58.310 --> 10:59.630
True to myself.

11:07.680 --> 11:08.230
Otoya.

11:09.160 --> 11:10.020
Wh-What?

11:10.020 --> 11:12.440
Are you having trouble with the lyrics?

11:13.040 --> 11:15.970
Yeah. I'm not sure what to write.

11:16.550 --> 11:17.730
But I'm fine.

11:17.730 --> 11:23.260
Isn't it more like you to write exactly
what you feel rather than think about it?

11:24.840 --> 11:26.410
Like me, huh?

11:26.410 --> 11:27.290
What?

11:28.200 --> 11:32.500
Maybe I'll go for a walk for a change of pace.

11:41.710 --> 11:43.140
Otoyan.

11:44.100 --> 11:45.240
Rei-chan.

11:45.240 --> 11:46.970
Long time, no see.

11:48.680 --> 11:51.950
Why are you here today? Aren't you on tour?

11:51.950 --> 11:55.230
I came to see Kohai-chan about Triple S.

11:55.230 --> 11:58.530
Triple S? Your song is already ready?

11:58.530 --> 12:02.240
Yeah. We're practicing right now.

12:02.240 --> 12:05.270
I see. That sounds fun.

12:06.440 --> 12:08.050
You're not having fun?

12:08.050 --> 12:08.830
What?

12:08.830 --> 12:10.370
I-It's not like that.

12:10.370 --> 12:15.120
Really? Then where's your usual smile?

12:15.120 --> 12:17.900
You were looking down
while you were walking earlier.

12:17.900 --> 12:19.340
That's not like—

12:19.340 --> 12:21.590
Am I not like myself unless I'm smiling?

12:23.670 --> 12:24.840
Otoyan?

12:24.840 --> 12:27.580
Uh, I'm talking about my lyrics.

12:27.580 --> 12:29.510
The lyrics I'm thinking of are like that.

12:29.510 --> 12:31.640
Otoyan, are you okay?

12:31.950 --> 12:36.150
I'm fine. All I can do is be myself.

12:39.580 --> 12:41.530
I'm really fine.

12:41.530 --> 12:43.110
I've gotta go.

12:46.320 --> 12:48.570
Isn't that Ittoki Otoya of STARISH?

12:48.570 --> 12:49.950
He's so cool.

12:49.950 --> 12:52.750
But I'm amazed he can walk around
by himself without a disguise.

13:00.330 --> 13:01.880
What did you want to talk about?

13:01.880 --> 13:04.180
Did you write any lyrics after that?

13:04.180 --> 13:05.510
Sorry. Not yet.

13:05.510 --> 13:07.060
I'm not blaming you.

13:07.520 --> 13:09.760
You're probably in the middle of facing yourself

13:09.760 --> 13:12.280
so you can write lyrics worthy of that song.

13:14.170 --> 13:15.140
I have a suggestion.

13:15.960 --> 13:20.840
Why don't we hold a training camp
at Raging Entertainment's studio?

13:20.840 --> 13:22.820
A training camp? Now?

13:23.150 --> 13:25.720
I'll make arrangements
for everything we'll need.

13:26.210 --> 13:29.500
Naturally, I've received
Shining Saotome's consent as well.

13:30.510 --> 13:32.220
It's not long until the recording session.

13:32.650 --> 13:35.040
Wouldn't you like to make some progress?

13:37.830 --> 13:40.000
Did something happen to Otoyan recently?

13:40.000 --> 13:42.800
He seems busy with the duet project.

13:43.170 --> 13:44.900
Is something wrong with Ikki?

13:44.900 --> 13:48.850
I just ran into him,
and he was acting strange.

13:48.850 --> 13:51.110
Kotobuki-san, you also think so?

13:51.110 --> 13:52.510
Do you have any ideas?

13:52.510 --> 13:55.430
No, but he does seem a little different.

13:56.040 --> 13:59.560
He felt like he was under a lot of stress.

13:59.560 --> 14:02.520
Lately, he's been acting
the same way at the dorms.

14:04.950 --> 14:08.780
In any case, I think you
should try talking to him.

14:15.410 --> 14:16.730
A training camp?

14:16.730 --> 14:20.920
He replied that Otori-san invited him,
and he won't be coming back tonight.

14:20.920 --> 14:23.170
Will he be all right on his own?

14:29.430 --> 14:32.680
Otoya, let me know if there's anything you need.

14:32.680 --> 14:33.560
Got it.

14:33.560 --> 14:37.270
Now let's begin this performance of souls!

14:37.270 --> 14:39.910
Ichinose Tokiya

14:45.790 --> 14:48.490
Otoya, why don't you take a break?

14:48.490 --> 14:50.320
I'm fine. Let me focus.

14:50.320 --> 14:53.980
But you haven't eaten
anything since this morning.

14:54.870 --> 14:57.250
You should take care of yourself.

14:58.510 --> 15:00.120
Sorry. I'll eat later.

15:01.630 --> 15:03.000
Don't push yourself too hard.

15:07.630 --> 15:08.640
It's done.

15:11.150 --> 15:12.770
This is Nanami.

15:13.220 --> 15:15.460
What? Right now?

15:15.460 --> 15:18.960
Oh, yes. I just finished.

15:18.960 --> 15:20.980
Yes, I'll send it to you.

15:25.910 --> 15:27.110
Marvelous.

15:27.480 --> 15:29.990
The goddess of luck is smiling on me!

15:30.610 --> 15:33.450
Dear Nanami Haruka,
This truly is a soul-shaking song.
This will awaken the real Otoya.
Otori Eiichi

15:45.420 --> 15:45.920
Rain?

15:48.520 --> 15:51.150
It's okay. I just have to be myself.

15:54.000 --> 15:55.350
What? A training camp?

15:55.860 --> 15:59.250
We thought he might have called you.

15:59.250 --> 16:01.700
I had no idea.

16:01.700 --> 16:03.290
He's not answering his phone, either.

16:03.290 --> 16:04.650
We can't get in touch with him.

16:05.440 --> 16:06.660
No way.

16:06.660 --> 16:07.650
Dear Nanami Haruka,
This truly is a soul-shaking song.
This will awaken the real Otoya.
Otori Eiichi

16:13.430 --> 16:15.660
None of these lyrics feel right.

16:16.930 --> 16:18.620
You're right. This isn't good enough.

16:19.760 --> 16:24.840
Why? I'm not lying to myself.

16:26.640 --> 16:27.470
Otoya.

16:28.360 --> 16:30.930
Let's go deeper into your heart.

16:31.780 --> 16:34.260
It must be sleeping there.

16:37.100 --> 16:38.170
A power outage?

16:38.170 --> 16:41.520
Perfect. Let's keep working.

16:41.520 --> 16:43.520
What are you talking about?

16:43.880 --> 16:48.110
The darkness is perfect
for looking at your own heart.

16:48.110 --> 16:49.570
You're not making any sense.

16:49.570 --> 16:52.400
Reveal your true self. Look at it.

16:54.230 --> 16:55.930
Your soul.

16:57.950 --> 16:59.330
Stop that.

17:00.470 --> 17:02.830
How would you know how I really feel?

17:04.150 --> 17:05.500
Your songs.

17:06.250 --> 17:08.590
We share the same soul.

17:08.590 --> 17:09.290
What?

17:09.830 --> 17:13.980
I feel everything you feel.

17:16.680 --> 17:23.700
The only person who can truly understand
your sadness and loneliness...

17:24.340 --> 17:25.570
...is me.

17:26.830 --> 17:29.690
Ittoki Otoya Investigation Report
Profile

17:33.240 --> 17:35.070
What is this?

17:36.030 --> 17:38.570
You've lost a lot of things.

17:39.730 --> 17:45.200
Your father, your mother, the people
who raised you, a warm place to belong.

17:46.220 --> 17:49.880
Everything you wanted is gone.

17:49.880 --> 17:50.750
You're wrong!

17:50.750 --> 17:51.820
Then look at this!

18:01.010 --> 18:02.760
A sunflower field?

18:03.340 --> 18:06.350
You're starved for love.

18:40.530 --> 18:44.260
Not wanting to lose more, you donned a mask.

18:44.940 --> 18:46.980
A false mask of smiles.

18:46.980 --> 18:50.060
I don't know what you're talking about.

18:50.450 --> 18:55.460
Your friends are noticing
that your smiles are fake.

18:55.460 --> 18:56.760
That's not true!

18:57.210 --> 18:59.150
My friends don't think that!

19:00.700 --> 19:02.320
It's fun being around you.

19:01.440 --> 19:02.950
Otoya.

19:02.320 --> 19:04.480
Your smiles heal those around you.

19:02.950 --> 19:05.350
Your smiles are the sun.

19:04.480 --> 19:06.530
You have the best smiles again today.

19:05.350 --> 19:06.010
Otoya.

19:06.010 --> 19:07.060
Otoya.

19:07.060 --> 19:07.910
Guys.

19:08.490 --> 19:10.370
Your smiles are fantastic.

19:10.800 --> 19:12.920
They are the signposts that light our way.

19:13.260 --> 19:14.130
Tokiya.

19:14.900 --> 19:17.420
But they're a lie?

19:19.320 --> 19:20.840
I'm disappointed.

19:21.420 --> 19:23.010
I trusted you.

19:23.600 --> 19:25.240
You're a liar.

19:25.760 --> 19:28.640
I can't believe you're even smiling now.

19:29.000 --> 19:30.980
I don't want to be around you anymore.

19:33.680 --> 19:36.900
What are you talking about? I...

19:38.480 --> 19:39.460
Nanami.

19:52.160 --> 19:53.540
You're alone.

19:53.540 --> 19:54.410
No.

19:54.410 --> 19:56.320
Face your true self.

19:55.480 --> 19:57.420
No, no, no, no, no.

19:58.920 --> 20:01.130
Where is everyone?

20:13.520 --> 20:15.950
Let's go see the sunflowers together.

20:16.570 --> 20:17.820
It's a promise.

20:20.340 --> 20:22.400
No. Don't go.

20:23.290 --> 20:27.280
I understand. You want
to have the things you want.

20:27.740 --> 20:31.450
No matter what it takes.
No matter how it turns out.

20:31.450 --> 20:32.820
You still want it.

20:34.750 --> 20:35.930
I'm the same.

20:41.630 --> 20:43.840
Now let's sing together.

21:14.160 --> 21:19.520
Tear off that smiling mask

21:19.520 --> 21:24.340
You'll see a menacing and desolate world

21:24.700 --> 21:29.180
The sunflowers in the darkness

21:29.180 --> 21:37.680
Are torn to pieces as my song burns

21:39.310 --> 21:42.640
Don't hide the scars from your past

21:42.640 --> 21:44.890
My hidden scabs

21:44.890 --> 21:49.910
Find your true self

21:49.910 --> 21:52.540
Isn't it beautiful

21:52.540 --> 21:55.680
From this prison of loneliness

21:55.680 --> 21:57.960
Release me (release you)

21:57.960 --> 22:00.080
Now reach out your hand

22:00.080 --> 22:05.870
NEXT DOOR are the screams of my naked heart

22:05.870 --> 22:11.180
NEXT DOOR Where does it lead
(to the next paradise)

22:11.180 --> 22:13.680
My soul falls (rise up)

22:13.680 --> 22:16.540
With our voices as one

22:16.540 --> 22:24.440
Unleashing our true emotions, we sing for you

24:06.090 --> 24:07.580
My soul is trembling.

24:07.580 --> 24:09.780
This is the true sound of your soul.

24:09.780 --> 24:11.130
Uta Pri!
